WEBVTT

00:00:03.070 --> 00:00:05.840
You can run most of these conversations yourself.

00:00:05.890 --> 00:00:07.660
That’s the point of this course.

00:00:07.710 --> 00:00:12.240
But there are moments when an outside facilitator makes a real difference.

00:00:12.290 --> 00:00:15.200
The first is when the topic is about you.

00:00:15.250 --> 00:00:24.880
If the team needs to talk about leadership, about decisions you made, or about a conflict you’re part of, you can’t facilitate and take part honestly at the same time.

00:00:24.930 --> 00:00:28.620
Someone else should hold the room, so you can be a team member.

00:00:28.670 --> 00:00:31.320
The second is when trust is low.

00:00:31.370 --> 00:00:40.320
After a difficult reorganisation, a conflict, or a period where people left, people may not speak openly with their manager in the room guiding the process.

00:00:40.370 --> 00:00:42.300
A neutral person helps.

00:00:42.350 --> 00:00:44.900
The third is when the stakes are high.

00:00:44.950 --> 00:00:48.980
A new leadership team, a strategy, a merger of two teams.

00:00:49.030 --> 00:00:54.380
When the outcome matters a lot, it’s worth having someone whose only job is the process.

00:00:54.430 --> 00:00:57.740
And the fourth is simply when you want to take part fully.

00:00:57.790 --> 00:01:04.800
For many leaders, the most valuable thing about an outside facilitator is that they get to think, instead of running the session.

00:01:04.850 --> 00:01:09.380
An outside facilitator doesn’t have to be expensive or external to the company.

00:01:09.430 --> 00:01:14.200
It can be a colleague from another team, someone from HR, or an internal coach.

00:01:14.250 --> 00:01:18.660
You could even swap: you facilitate their team, they facilitate yours.

00:01:18.710 --> 00:01:25.500
And of course, if you’d like help from me, you can find out more under “Work with Michael” on formyourteam.dk.

00:01:25.550 --> 00:01:27.420
Thank you for taking this course.

00:01:27.470 --> 00:01:31.920
I hope your team gets as much out of these conversations as the teams I’ve worked with.

00:01:31.970 --> 00:01:33.245
Good luck, and enjoy it.

